From: Project Luma <luma@project-luma.org>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a810: disable IFPC for the FP6 diagnostic build

The Fairphone 6 A810 currently enters a repeatable GPU hang under a native
Waydroid workload.  Recovery then reports that the CX GDSC did not collapse
and that the GMU GPU_SET OOB request timed out.

Keep every other A810 capability unchanged, but disable idle power collapse
for the first controlled diagnostic.  This deliberately trades idle power for
stability and is not intended for release unless physical testing establishes
that IFPC is the initiating condition.

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c
index 3e6f409d1..bad552bbe 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c
@@ -2459,8 +2459,7 @@ static const struct adreno_info a8xx_gpus[] = {
 		.inactive_period = DRM_MSM_INACTIVE_PERIOD,
 		.quirks = ADRENO_QUIRK_HAS_CACHED_COHERENT |
 			  ADRENO_QUIRK_HAS_HW_APRIV |
-			  ADRENO_QUIRK_PREEMPTION |
-			  ADRENO_QUIRK_IFPC,
+			  ADRENO_QUIRK_PREEMPTION,
 		.funcs = &a8xx_gpu_funcs,
 		.zapfw = "gen80300_zap.mbn",
 		.a6xx = &(const struct a6xx_info) {
-- 
2.51.0
